From: Broyojo <dha@xoba.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:28:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Set Wine's present rect for a fullscreen window, and test
 a view's cover against its bounds

Entering exclusive fullscreen, on a Reset that keeps it and on reactivation,
tell win32u where the frame is presented (D3DKMT_ESCAPE_SET_PRESENT_RECT_WINE),
and clear it on leaving, as Wine's own D3D does. Under an emulated mode whose
shape differs from the screen's, win32u then maps the window to the whole
monitor, so the window covers the screen instead of staying an ordinary
window under the menu bar.

The cover test that clears the window's background used the view's visible
rectangle alone, which a view that does not clip to its bounds (the default
since macOS 14) reports larger than itself; a letterboxed view then passed
for covering its window and the desktop showed through around it. A view now
covers only where its bounds do too, and a background a pass cleared while the
view covered is made opaque black again once it no longer does.

Work in progress: Wine's Mac driver still clips and places the letterboxed
client area wrongly, so a 16:9 mode on a 3024x1964 panel is not yet right.
---
 unix/unix/src/metal/macdrv.rs  | 34 ++++++++++++++----
 windows/d3d9/src/fullscreen.rs | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

